				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">03</span>
					<h3>Creating a Will</h3>
					<p>Preparing a Will is one of the most important steps you can take to protect your loved ones and ensure your wishes are respected after your death.

                       A carefully prepared Will allows you to decide how your assets and estate will be distributed among your family, friends and other beneficiaries. 
                       It also enables you to nominate guardians for your children under the age of 18, appoint trusted individuals to administer your estate, 
                       and record your wishes regarding funeral arrangements, burial or cremation.

                       Having a properly drafted Will provides peace of mind, helps minimise uncertainty and potential disputes, and ensures your loved ones are 
                       provided for in accordance with your intentions.</p>
                    
